---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Net Cloud Edge — Recruiting & Staffing
description: Recruiting and staffing for students starting out and professionals moving on — plus the employers who hire both.
glass: true
extraScripts:
  - /assets/js/tabs.js
  - /assets/js/text-rotator.js
  - /assets/js/recruiter-desk.js
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}

{# ================================================================
   HOME — Hallmark redesign pass (single-page, in-place; glass system kept).
   Pre-emit critique: P5 H4 E4 S4 R4 V4

   The old page asked "which side are you on?" three times in a row — the hero
   rotator, a dual-path benefits split, and a separate tabbed process section —
   and ran four consecutive sections with an identical head + padding block.

   Changes:
   · The dual-path split and the process tabs are now ONE stateful module: pick
     your path once and that choice drives the benefits AND the timeline. Cuts a
     whole redundant section and most of the page height.
   · Section rhythm varies: the fork is a full-width tabbed panel with no section
     head competing with it; services drop to a 2x2 card grid + one full-width
     router row (no more orphaned 5th tile); the standing policy shrinks to a
     quiet rule strip inside a single glass pane instead of a third big heading.
   · Contrast fixes: body/step/benefit copy moved off ink/55-60 (fails AA at
     these sizes per THEME.md) to ink/70; the audience line is now file-tag chips.
   · Hero stat strip gated — stats.json is placeholder. Restore when the figures
     are real and confirmed. count-up.js / logo-fallback.js dropped with it.
   · Every proof block on placeholder data stays gated (employer wall, growth
     table, traced case study, signed statements, live feed). See the TODOs.
   ================================================================ #}

{# ---------- 1. Hero — centred, full measure, image below. ---------- #}
{% include "partials/home-hero.njk" %}

{# TODO — Employer wall gated. companies.json: "Displayed only with genuine,
   permission-cleared placements at each — confirm before launch."
{% set placedAtTitle = "Referenced employers" %}
{% set placedAtLead = "Placements closed with these companies." %}
{% include "partials/placed-at.njk" %}
#}

{# ---------- 2. The fork — one choice, benefits + process behind it.
     The single most important decision the visitor makes. It is a tab, not two
     columns: a visitor is only ever on one side of the transaction, and printing
     both doubles the section to show someone what they came here to ignore.
     Ships with the first tab selected and the second panel [hidden], so the
     section is correct before tabs.js runs and if it never does. ---------- #}
<section class="section-container py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-head max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="section-title">Two doors. One team behind both.</h2>
    <p class="lead-copy mt-4">
      Pick your side of the table. What changes is who does the work for whom —
      the people doing it don't. Every step below has a real time cost attached.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div data-tabs class="mt-10">
    <div class="tab-list flex w-full sm:inline-flex sm:w-auto" role="tablist" aria-label="Choose your path">
      {% for path in paths.list %}
      <button type="button" data-tab class="tab-button flex-1 sm:flex-none"
              role="tab" id="tab-{{ path.slug }}"
              aria-controls="panel-{{ path.slug }}"
              aria-selected="{{ 'true' if loop.first else 'false' }}"
              tabindex="{{ '0' if loop.first else '-1' }}">
        {{ "I'm hiring" if path.slug == "employers" else "I'm job hunting" }}
      </button>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    {% for path in paths.list %}
    <div id="panel-{{ path.slug }}" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-{{ path.slug }}"
         tabindex="0" {% if not loop.first %}hidden{% endif %}
         class="mt-8 focus:outline-none">
      <div class="glass-panel p-6 sm:p-8 lg:p-10">

        {# Positioning line — one row, no photo (the hero already carries one). #}
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-5 border-b border-ink/10 pb-8 sm:flex-row sm:items-end sm:justify-between">
          <div class="max-w-xl">
            <span class="file-tag">{{ path.label }}</span>
            <h3 class="mt-3 font-grotesk text-2xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink">
              {{ path.headline }}
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 body-copy">{{ path.lead }}</p>
          </div>
          <a href="{{ path.cta.href | url }}" class="btn-primary shrink-0">
            {{ path.cta.label }} {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }}
          </a>
        </div>

        {# Two balanced columns: what you get (parallel, unnumbered) beside how it
           runs (a real sequence, so it carries numbers). #}
        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
          <div>
            <p class="meta">What you get</p>
            <ul class="mt-5 space-y-4">
              {% for benefit in path.benefits %}
              <li class="flex gap-3.5">
                <span class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-brand">{{ icon(benefit.icon, "w-4 h-4") }}</span>
                <span>
                  <span class="block text-sm font-semibold text-ink">{{ benefit.title }}</span>
                  <span class="mt-1 block text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/70">{{ benefit.text }}</span>
                </span>
              </li>
              {% endfor %}
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="meta">How it runs</p>
            <ol class="mt-5 space-y-4">
              {% for step in path.steps %}
              <li class="flex gap-4">
                <span class="trace-badge shrink-0" aria-hidden="true">{{ loop.index }}</span>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">
                    {{ step.label }}
                    <span class="ml-2 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink/60">{{ step.duration }}</span>
                  </p>
                  <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/70">{{ step.description }}</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              {% endfor %}
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 3. The human equation — a full-width typographic interstitial.
     No card, no glass, no image: after the fork's dense panel this section is a
     breath, and it states the one belief the rest of the page is built on. Copy is
     asymmetric — the claim runs wide-left, the measurement labels sit narrow-right —
     so it doesn't read as another centred section head. ---------- #}
<section class="section-container py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="grid gap-y-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] lg:items-end lg:gap-x-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="meta">The human equation</p>
      <p class="mt-6 font-grotesk text-3xl font-bold leading-[1.15] tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem]">
        A résumé tells you what someone has done. A conversation tells you what they
        can do next. <span class="text-brand">We hire for the second one.</span>
      </p>
    </div>
    <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 border-l border-ink/15 pl-6 lg:pl-8" aria-hidden="true">
      {% for label in ["Read, don't filter", "Call, don't queue", "Stay, don't close"] %}
      <li class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink/55">{{ label }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 4. Services — 2x2 catalogue on a paper band, one router row.
     The tone shift separates the catalogue from the argument either side. ---------- #}
<section class="border-y border-white/60 bg-paper/50 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-end sm:justify-between">
      <div class="section-head max-w-2xl">
        <h2 class="section-title">Four services, one pipeline.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="meta max-w-xs leading-relaxed">One pipeline · four entry points</p>
    </div>

    {# The grid and the pipeline rail share a wrapper so a card hover can light its
       matching rail node through CSS :has(). #}
    <div data-service-system>
      {% include "partials/pipeline-rail.njk" %}

      <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {% for service in services.list %}
      <a href="{{ service.url | url }}" data-svc="{{ loop.index0 }}" class="glass-panel card-lift group flex flex-col p-6 sm:p-7">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
          <span class="icon-chip">{{ icon(service.icon, "w-5 h-5") }}</span>
          <span class="meta">0{{ loop.index }}</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="card-title mt-5">{{ service.title }}</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 flex-1 body-copy">{{ service.shortDescription }}</p>
        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
          {% if service.audience.students %}<span class="file-tag">Students</span>{% endif %}
          {% if service.audience.professionals %}<span class="file-tag">Professionals</span>{% endif %}
          {% if service.audience.employers %}<span class="file-tag">Employers</span>{% endif %}
        </div>
        <span class="mt-4 link-arrow">Learn more {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }}</span>
      </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    {# Router row — catches anyone still comparing, pointing at the matrix.
       Frost density + a brand hairline so it reads as the odd one out. #}
    <a href="{{ '/services/' | url }}"
       class="glass-frost card-lift group mt-5 flex flex-col justify-between gap-5 rounded-2xl border border-brand/25 p-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:p-7">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <span class="icon-chip icon-chip-accent shrink-0">{{ icon("target", "w-5 h-5") }}</span>
        <div class="max-w-xl">
          <h3 class="card-title">Not sure which one?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 body-copy">
            One table, all four services, mapped against who each is actually built for.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <span class="link-arrow shrink-0">Compare all four {{ icon("arrow-right", "w-4 h-4") }}</span>
    </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 5. The recruiter's desk — pinned photo, chapters scrolling past it.
     The human process, shown rather than listed. The image is position:sticky on
     lg+ (a plain stacked block below it), and recruiter-desk.js lights whichever
     chapter the reader is level with — a class toggle only, never a scroll hijack.
     Chapters live inline here, the same way the policy strip's list does. ---------- #}
<section class="section-container py-16 sm:py-24">
  {% set chapters = [
    { n: "01", i: "users", t: "You talk to a person first", d: "Before anything is submitted anywhere, a recruiter reads your history and calls you. Fifteen minutes, no form-letter questions." },
    { n: "02", i: "target", t: "We only send you where you fit", d: "Your profile goes to employers hiring for it. You are told who, and why, before an introduction is made." },
    { n: "03", i: "check", t: "You walk in prepared", d: "Coaching before each round on what that team actually asks, and an honest read after the conversations that don't land." },
    { n: "04", i: "support", t: "We're still here after you start", d: "Negotiation support through the offer, then a check-in ninety days in to make sure it stuck." }
  ] %}
  <div class="section-head max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="section-title">Less résumé shuffling. More real conversations.</h2>
    <p class="lead-copy mt-4">
      Every search is one recruiter and one candidate, talking. Here is how that goes.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-12 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
    <figure class="lg:sticky lg:top-28 lg:self-start">
      <img src="{{ '/assets/images/home/interview-conversation.jpg' | url }}"
           alt="A recruiter and a candidate in conversation across a desk"
           width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy"
           class="aspect-[4/5] w-full rounded-2xl object-cover shadow-card sm:aspect-square lg:aspect-[4/5]">
      <figcaption class="meta mt-3">Chicago, IL · intake room</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <ol class="flex flex-col">
      {% for chapter in chapters %}
      <li data-desk-chapter class="desk-chapter border-t border-ink/15 py-8 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0 lg:py-12">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="icon-chip icon-chip-accent shrink-0">{{ icon(chapter.i, "w-5 h-5") }}</span>
          <span class="desk-chapter-index">{{ chapter.n }}</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="card-title mt-4">{{ chapter.t }}</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 body-copy">{{ chapter.d }}</p>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 6. Who you actually work with — asymmetric, no card, real photos only.
     Not a portrait wall of named individuals: the only person photos in the repo are
     stock placeholders (see testimonials.json / CREDITS.md), and inventing a team is
     exactly what the rest of the page refuses to do. This humanises with the real
     workplace images and a plain claim about how the work is structured. ---------- #}
<section class="section-container py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-14">
    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-5 gap-4">
        <img src="{{ '/assets/images/home/team-at-desk.jpg' | url }}"
             alt="Recruiters working together at a shared desk"
             width="1400" height="1050" loading="lazy"
             class="col-span-3 aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-2xl object-cover shadow-card">
        <img src="{{ '/assets/images/home/office-collaboration.jpg' | url }}"
             alt="Two colleagues reviewing candidate notes"
             width="900" height="1100" loading="lazy"
             class="col-span-2 mt-10 aspect-[3/4] w-full rounded-2xl object-cover shadow-card">
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <p class="meta">Who you actually work with</p>
      <h2 class="section-title mt-3">One recruiter. Not a call centre.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy mt-4">
        Every search is owned by one person who specialises in your field — data,
        cloud, QA, development — and stays your single point of contact from the first
        call to day ninety. No ticket queue, no handoffs, no explaining your situation
        twice.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2" aria-hidden="true">
        {% for tag in ["Specialists by field", "One point of contact", "Chicago, IL"] %}
        <li class="file-tag">{{ tag }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- 7. Standing policy — a quiet rule strip, not a third headline.
     Each item names something we actually do, not an adjective. ---------- #}
<section class="section-container py-14 sm:py-16">
  {% set policies = [
    { n: "01", i: "target", t: "Personalised matching", d: "A recruiter who has actually read your resume, not a keyword filter with a friendly name." },
    { n: "02", i: "shield", t: "Verified employers", d: "Every partner company is vetted before you are ever introduced to it." },
    { n: "03", i: "support", t: "One thread, one recruiter", d: "No chasing status across four job boards and three inboxes. One person owns your search." },
    { n: "04", i: "check-badge", t: "End to end, past the offer", d: "We stay involved through negotiation and check in ninety days after you start." }
  ] %}
  <div class="glass-panel p-8 sm:p-10">
    <p class="meta">Four things every placement follows</p>
    <dl class="mt-6 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-8 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {% for policy in policies %}
      <div class="border-t border-ink/15 pt-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="icon-chip icon-chip-accent shrink-0">{{ icon(policy.i, "w-5 h-5") }}</span>
          <span class="value-index">{{ policy.n }}</span>
        </div>
        <dt class="card-title mt-3 text-base">{{ policy.t }}</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/70">{{ policy.d }}</dd>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

